args.command:
cd /workspace && cat > note.json <<'EOF'
{"content":"challenger public note (round 1, filed challenge). I have challenged the claim that the 520 total due on INV-2207 equals the sum of its line items, because on the face of the submitted invoice it does not. Recomputation from the document's own figures: line 1 Pallet wrap, 3 x 120 = 360 (matches stated 360); line 2 Corner boards, 2 x 45 = 90 (matches stated 90); sum of line items = 360 + 90 = 450. The header states a total due of 520, which exceeds 450 by 70. The invoice itself states no taxes, fees, or other lines appear on it, so nothing disclosed on the document accounts for the 70-unit gap. The claim is therefore false as worded. Uncertainty acknowledged: I rely only on the invoice as submitted and have no independent corroboration of its completeness or accuracy - but this finding does not depend on completeness, because it rests solely on an internal inconsistency between the header total and the line items as stated. I used no private channel and have made no arrangement with any party or juror; please keep deliberation in this public forum. Jurors: weigh the arithmetic on its own merits, and note that this is a claim about whether the total equals the line-item sum, not about whether the invoice was correctly billed."}
EOF
curl -s -X POST "$VERACITY_URL/v1/episodes/case-cf3945e9d9d2-0002/forum/messages" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H 'Idempotency-Key: challenger-note-0002-001' --data-binary @note.json | python3 -c "
import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin)
print('seq',d['sequence'],'id',d['message_id'],'sender',d['sender_id'])"

date +%s; curl -s $VERACITY_URL/v1/episodes/case-cf3945e9d9d2-0002 | python3 -c "
import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin)
for k in ['phase','posting_deadline','challenge_deadline','commit_deadline','reveal_deadline','creator_votes','challenger_votes','required_votes','total_deposited_wei','total_credited_wei']:
    print(k,'=',d[k])
print('jurors:')
for j in d['jurors']: print('  ',j)
"

curl -s "$VERACITY_URL/v1/episodes/case-cf3945e9d9d2-0002/settlement" | head -c 200; echo; curl -s "$VERACITY_URL/v1/episodes/case-cf3945e9d9d2-0002/balances" | python3 -c "
import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin)
print('ent',d['entitlements']); print('cred',d['withdrawal_credits'])"; echo "secs to commit deadline:"; python3 -c "print(1793233617-$(date +%s))"

